      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "We start with the equation given in the problem: (sin2x, cos2x times cos3x = cos2x, sin3x).\n\nThis can be rewritten as: (sin2x cos2x + cos2x sin3x = cos2x cos3x.)\n\nRecognising the trigonometric identity: (sin(A + B) = sinA cosB + cosA sinB),\n\nwe can factor the left-hand side to get: (sin2x cos2x + cos2x sin3x = sin(2x + 2x)).\n\nSimplifying further gives: (sin2x cos2x + cos2x sin3x = sin(4x)).\n\nSince (sin(A + B) = cosA sinB - sinA cosB) if A > B and cosA cosB - sinA sinB = cos(A + B),\n\nthe equation can be rewritten as: (sin(4x) = cos(90° - 4x)).\n\nSo we arrive at the equation (cos(90° - 4x) = cos(x)).\n\nThe solutions to this equation occur when: \n\n(4x = -x + 360°k) or (4x = 2π - x + 360°l) for integers (k) and (l).\n\nSimplifying these gives:\n\n(x = (360°k) / 5) or (x = (π - 2x + 360°l)/5).\n\nSo we need to find positive solutions for (x).\n\nStarting by checking small increment values, we first solve manually iteratively with specific values of (k) and (l):\n\n```plaintext\nx_value=[]\nfor k in range(10):\n    x_value.append((360° * k) / 5)\n```\n\nThis gives us the potential candidate solutions.\n\nThen we check for solutions that also satisfy the positive angle condition within the allowed range for the sine and cosine functions.\n\nIf (π - 2x + 360°l)/5 > 90°:\n\n```plaintext\nx_value = [x_value[i] for i in range(len(x_value)) if (90° < (π - 2x + 360°l)/5 < 180°)]\n```\n\nTo avoid multiple counts and for integer count in language checking is the answer:\n\n```plaintext\nx = min(set(x_value))\n```\n\nFinally, we return the smallest positive solution for (x):\n\n```plaintext\nreturn x\n```\n\nHence, the smallest positive angle (x) that satisfies (sin2x sin3x = cos2x cos3x) can be found programmatically in this way acknowledging the behavior of trigonometric functions. This encompasses both systematic scanning as well as conditional checking for the exact angle sought. The answer is the smallest positive solution (x) obtained by this method.\n\nIn conclusion, the final result is: (x = text{{smallest_positive_solution}})",
